{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: dominant factor is a low-kurtosis premium, robust at 60d and 250d and in own-history ts_z form (each 1.2-1.3 standalone, plateau across horizons and specs). Secondary factor is 20-60d reversal, best own-history normalized as ts_z(ret(40),120). Blending kurt(60), kurt(250), ts_z(kurt(60),120) with the ts_z reversal gives a broad flat ridge near SR 2.0 that survives component swaps, weight tilts, window perturbations, and delay-3 (SR 1.93). Final picks are the same 4-component composite in three combining conventions (raw sum, cs_z, cs_rank) to hedge scale-convention risk on the holdout while staying at the top of the ridge. Deliberately avoided single-peak variants without plateau support.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:34:24.494386+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["add(sub(neg(kurt(60)), kurt(250)), sub(neg(ts_z(kurt(60), 120)), ts_z(ret(40), 120)))", "add(cs_z(sub(neg(kurt(60)), kurt(250))), cs_z(sub(neg(ts_z(kurt(60), 120)), ts_z(ret(40), 120))))", "add(cs_rank(sub(neg(kurt(60)), kurt(250))), cs_rank(sub(neg(ts_z(kurt(60), 120)), ts_z(ret(40), 120))))"], "chosen_sr_train": [2.0768, 2.0761, 2.0684], "rationale": "Composite of a low-kurtosis premium (short long assets with high 60d and 250d return kurtosis, in level and own-history ts_z form) plus 40d reversal normalized by own 120d history. Family shows a broad flat train ridge near SR 2.0 across horizons, weights, and normalizations, with mild delay-3 decay (1.93), indicating genuine factors rather than a noise spike. The three picks are the same 4-component signal under raw, cs_z, and cs_rank combining conventions to hedge scale-convention risk out of sample.", "n_batches_used": 9, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:34:30.617327+00:00"}
